From 1bcbc6acfbf3b848be92867cd0310ec2a40670bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 07:52:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add Form window-placement surface

Closes API-COMPLETENESS.md P2 item 6 (Form section 5.1): DesktopBounds,
DesktopLocation, SetDesktopBounds, SetDesktopLocation, MaximizedBounds,
RestoreBounds, RightToLeftLayout and the MaximizedBoundsChanged /
RightToLeftLayoutChanged events with their OnXxx raisers - designer-emitted
placement code did not compile without them.

Desktop coordinates coincide with the form's Bounds on this layer, so those
delegate; MaximizedBounds and RightToLeftLayout are stored with change events;
RestoreBounds returns the normal-state bounds, tracked by a minimal capture in
the WindowState setter (record on the first move away from Normal, hold across a
Minimized<->Maximized switch, clear when Normal again).

Covered by FormPlacementFunctionalTests (property round-trips, change events,
desktop-coordinate delegation, RestoreBounds while Normal). Full Forms suite
green at 2470.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
